agsbuild: deep-copy task strings to avoid a reference count race

AGS::Common::String shares its buffer between copies with a reference count
that is not thread-safe. TaskPipedProcess and TaskDeleteFiles kept shallow
copies of their parameters, so the tool paths (e.g. the agscc path, shared by
every script compile task) were copied and released concurrently on the worker
threads. The count went wrong and agsbuild sporadically crashed with SIGSEGV
in ~Task / ~TaskManager after the build had finished.

Clone the params and file lists like the other tasks already do for their
names, inputs and lists.

Upstream PR: not opened yet (branch fix-agsbuild-params-thread-race in the fork).

diff --git a/Tools/agsbuild/taskmanager.cpp b/Tools/agsbuild/taskmanager.cpp
index 2c20fa492..0e8d13e22 100644
--- a/Tools/agsbuild/taskmanager.cpp
+++ b/Tools/agsbuild/taskmanager.cpp
@@ -257,16 +257,23 @@ HError TaskWriteStringList::RunImpl()
 // TaskPipedProcess
 //-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
 
+// The params are deep-copied: String's reference count is not thread-safe, and the tool paths
+// are shared by many tasks which copy them on their own threads.
+static PipedProcessParams Clone(const PipedProcessParams &params)
+{
+    return PipedProcessParams(params.ExePath.Clone(), params.Params.Clone(), params.OutputToStdOut);
+}
+
 TaskPipedProcess::TaskPipedProcess(const String &name, ITaskManager *mgr, const PipedProcessParams &params)
     : Task(name, mgr)
-    , _params(params)
+    , _params(Clone(params))
 {
 }
 
 TaskPipedProcess::TaskPipedProcess(const String &name, ITaskManager *mgr, const PipedProcessParams &params,
     const std::vector<TaskInput> &input_tasks)
     : Task(name, mgr, input_tasks)
-    , _params(params)
+    , _params(Clone(params))
 {
 }
 
